        }
        debug { }
    }
    compileOptions { sourceCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_17; targetCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_17 }
    kotlin { jvmToolchain(17) }  // hmm inside android block: kotlinOptions is deprecated in AGP 8.13? Use `kotlin { compilerOptions { jvmTarget } }` at top level.
    buildFeatures { compose = true }
    packaging { resources { excludes += "/META-INF/{AL2.0,LGPL2.1}" } }
}

dependencies { ... }
```

For Kotlin jvmTarget with AGP 8.13 + KGP 2.4, recommended: top-level
```kotlin
kotlin {
    compilerOptions {
        jvmTarget.set(org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.dsl.JvmTarget.JVM_17)
    }
}
```
jvmToolchain(17) is also fine but requires toolchain provisioning; since JDK 17 is the running JDK, it resolves automatically. I'll use compilerOptions + sourceCompatibility 17 to be safe (no toolchain download).

Let me write it.

Version: package.json version is 1.1.7 → native major rewrite → 2.0.0. versionCode = 2*10000+0*100+0 = 20000 to match the convention from the release commit. Good, keeps continuity (Android can install over 1.1.7 which had versionCode 1.1.7*... = 10107).

Manifest: permissions — INTERNET, ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE, READ_MEDIA_IMAGES/AUDIO/VIDEO (API 33+), READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE (maxSdk 32), FOREGROUND_SERVICE? Not needed. Also `android:requestLegacyExternalStorage` no. Add `usesCleartextTraffic` false. Add FileProvider for sharing exported files.

ML Kit bundled text-recognition: meta-data com.google.mlkit.vision.DEPENDENCIES? For bundled models, add:
```xml
<meta-data android:name="com.google.mlkit.vision.DEPENDENCIES" android:value="ocr" />
```
Actually for the bundled `com.google.mlkit:text-recognition`, no meta-data is needed (that's for unbundled play-services-mlkit variants). Bundled includes latin model. For Cyrillic, bundled latin model includes Cyrillic? ML Kit's Latin recognizer supports Latin script + also Cyrillic? The Latin script recognition model supports Latin, Cyrillic, and Devanagari? Per docs: "Latin script recognition" supports Latin alphabet; the bundled model also recognizes Cyrillic and Georgian? I recall ML Kit Latin recognizer supports Latin, Cyrillic, Devanagari, Bengali, Thai, Japanese/Korean? Hmm. ML Kit docs: text-recognition (Latin) — supports Latin script. And separate models exist for Chinese, Devanagari, Japanese, Korean. Latin model: "Recognizes Latin script" — but I believe the bundled Latin recognizer covers Latin + Cyrillic + digits + punctuation. To be safe, note it in the report and allow the AI vision fallback for other scripts.

